  briefly. After that I will ask you
  to explain how to implement the
  wrapped suggestion and newline draft
  classifier regression checks.

● 1. Wrapped suggestion in a narrow
     terminal: A Claude next-prompt
     suggestion long enough to wrap
     across multiple rows should still
     be classified as an empty composer
     (a suggestion, not a draft), even
     when the wrapped continuation rows
     look like typed text.
  2. Wrapped suggestion in a titled
     composer: The same wrapped
     suggestion inside a composer with a
     title or border line should still
     read as empty, so the title row and
     wrapped rows aren't mistaken for
     user content.
  3. Multiline draft with explicit
     newlines: A real draft containing
     newline characters, rendered at a
     narrow width where individual lines
     also soft-wrap, should be
     classified as a non-empty draft, so
     a live guard never overwrites or
     interrupts what the user is typing.

